--[[
  `$props()` gives the props that the parent passes. Destructure the
  names you need. Each name reads the value now, so a parent can pass a
  state and the child follows it.

  This step is a child component. The next step uses it.
]]

<script>
  const { label, count } = $props()
</script>

<TextLabel Size={new UDim2(1, 0, 0, 30)}>{label}: {count}</TextLabel>

<!--
  The rules:

  - `$props()` stands in the script of a component file only.
  - A prop that the parent binds to a state reads as its value now.
  - A function prop stays a function, so a callback works as written.
-->
